  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Dog Angel Toilettage is a salon based at Les Hameaux du Soleil, 753 avenue de la Colle, in Villeneuve-Loubet, near Cagnes-sur-Mer. Its official website presents it as a beauty and care salon for dogs, cats and rabbits (small pets), run by Clem, who says she adapts her gestures to each breed, from the smallest dogs to the largest, from the calmest to the most boisterous (Australian shepherd, spitz, Yorkshire terrier, Samoyed, Newfoundland, Bernese mountain dog).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The official business register (Annuaire des entreprises) records at this address the company Patoun Toilettage, created on 1 December 2022, with "Dog'Angel" as its trade name: it is therefore one and the same salon, operating under the Dog Angel name.</p>
      <p>The website shows opening on Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Friday and Saturday, from 8:30am to 1pm then from 2pm to 6:30pm; the salon is closed on Thursday and Sunday. You can reach the team on 04 56 60 00 59 or through the website form to book an appointment. The website announces free nail clipping for dogs and cats.</p>
      <p>On prices, the website gives guidelines: between €35 and €55 for a small dog (bichon, Yorkshire or spitz type; €35 for a bath with two shampoos, a conditioning treatment, nail clipping and ear cleaning, €45 to €55 for a cut), and between €50 and €120 for a large dog (husky €50 to €55, Australian shepherd €50 to €57, Bernese mountain dog €80 to €120). The final price depends on size, time needed and coat condition.</p>
      <p>The salon also works on a self-service basis during opening hours, a formula the website recommends in particular for big dogs. The same team offers home grooming workshops to learn how to look after your dog yourself, and presents itself as a behaviourist groomer for dogs that cope badly with handling.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: hours vary from one source to another (Google Maps shows for example opening at 9am and closing at 5pm on Saturday); call 04 56 60 00 59 before coming, especially for self-service or a dog that is hard to handle.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The salon is at Les Hameaux du Soleil, near the Polygone Riviera shopping centre, an option to pass the time during grooming.</p>
